{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 102, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing the direct input-to-output edge leaves at most one path (via edge 4) to the output, so the drop is far larger (e.g. exp 43)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is absent, deleting edge 3 forces all signal through node 2, risking disconnection and much larger accuracy loss."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, cutting edge 0 kills both intermediate nodes, leaving only edge 3, so the penalty is much larger (exps 72, 100)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 absent, edge 1 is the only feed into the intermediate nodes, so removing it collapses the cell to edge 3 alone."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the first edge with a 3x3 conv adds much more capacity than replacing a skip (exps 9, 31, 35 vs 2, 67)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Avg-pooling on the input-output edge blurs the shortcut; swapping it for a conv gives large gains (exps 34, 48) versus small ones when replacing skip or 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the clean identity shortcut with pooling destroys the residual path that stabilizes training (exps 8, 83)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning the last conv into the output node into pooling removes key learnable 